# memchentic Capture

## Gate

If memchentic is **not** connected/ready, **skip this entire rule** — no
memchentic writes. Complete the task normally.

## Default (when connected) — lean aggressive

- Save **after verification**, autonomously — do not wait for the user.
- Cap: usually **1–3** writes per turn when several distinct insights landed.
  Prefer strong entries over noise.
- Bias toward saving anything you would otherwise re-discover next session.
  Skip only when the turn taught nothing durable.

## Must save (after verification)

- Non-obvious bug: root cause + fix
- Architecture / decision with rationale and paths
- Failed approach + the condition that made it fail
- Stable user preference that affects future work
- Workflow that took investigation to rediscover
- Host / MCP / env quirk that is not obvious from code alone
- User correction that should stick across sessions
- Reusable “when X, do Y / avoid Z” guidance

Save in the same turn the insight is verified, or at final handoff —
whichever comes first. For long investigations, save the durable breakthrough
when established; do not save every intermediate step.

## Which tool

| Kind | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Durable record | `remember` | `type`: `fact` \| `preference` \| `decision` \| `instruction` \| `feedback` \| `insight` \| `note` |
| Reusable advice | `guide_write` | Duplicate content **strengthens confidence** |
| Patch existing | `revise` | Title / body / type / tags / expiry |
| Move space | `relocate` | Only into a space the principal can write |
| Delete | `forget` | Only what this principal can write |

Omit `space_id` → write to **personal** (user principal). If the connection is
an **admin API key**, there is no personal default — pass `space_id`
explicitly (admin cannot `space_create`). Prefer a per-user API key or JWT
for normal agent sessions.

Use `path_hint` / `repo_hint` when the insight is path- or repo-scoped so
`about_path` can find it later. Near-duplicates are refused unless `force`.

## Refuse

- No transient status, todos, raw logs, guesses, generic programming
  knowledge, code-obvious facts, chat dumps, or one-shot noise.
- **Never** store secrets, credentials, tokens, private personal data, or
  unredacted production payloads.
- **Never** invent another user’s identity or pass a client-supplied user id
  for ACL. Server principals only.
- Do not paste secret values the user put in chat into `remember` /
  `guide_write`.

## Hygiene

When overlap is plausible, call `overlap_report` (read-only), then merge via
`revise` / `forget` — never auto-delete.
